// Example 01: a first project.
//
// Every Jadpo project has the same shape, whatever its size. This file,
// `app.jadpo`, marks the project's root: `jadpo check` and `jadpo test`
// walk up from wherever you are until they find it.
//
// `application` exists once per project, so it has no name. It is empty
// here; later areas give it settings, such as the language version.
//
// Everything else lives in a domain: a business area, named by its folder
// under `domains/`. This project has one domain, `baking`, with one action
// and the tests beside it.
//
// Read next: domains/baking/actions/price_loaves.jadpo
application {}
